@section Security
@note
  YUME 2.0 always uses ephemeral ML-KEM-1024 + X25519, a mandatory
  file-distributed PSK, per-message AES-256-GCM keys, and independent
  directional epochs. JSON security_mode selects extreme (default),
  normal, soft, or bounded ultimate limits; see docs/SECURITY_MODES.md.
@end

@section HTTP / Operator identity
--real-backend
--robots-deny
--real-index
--real-root
--real-secret-file
--operator-identity
--operator-proof-mode
--operator-proof-api
--operator-proof-token-file
--operator-ca-key
--operator-ca-cert
--operator-delegated-key
--operator-delegated-cert
@note
  The proof establishes CA-authorized operator identity, not a guarantee
  that the host cannot inspect or log client traffic. Display names are
  informational; clients trust the certificate chain and fingerprints.
@end

